  Fixture template for the fee_schedule paragraph type: every amount below
  is typed into the template itself, and the type has no configured fields.
#}
<table class="fee-schedule">
  <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Fee</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Pool day pass, resident</td><td class="fee">$3</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pool day pass, non-resident</td><td class="fee">$7</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pavilion rental, half day</td><td class="fee">$55</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pavilion rental, full day</td><td class="fee">$95</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Youth soccer league, per season</td><td class="fee">$38</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pickleball court, per hour</td><td class="fee">$6</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Community garden plot, per year</td><td class="fee">$22</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Kayak launch permit, annual</td><td class="fee">$18</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<div class="fee-notes">
  <p>Fees are set each spring by the district board and posted at every recreation center.</p>
  <p>Residents of the district pay the resident rate; bring proof of address to register.</p>
  <p>Fee waivers are available for households enrolled in approved assistance programs.</p>
  <p>Rentals booked fewer than 14 days ahead cannot be refunded, only rescheduled.</p>
  <p>Youth league fees include a jersey; financial aid covers the full fee on request.</p>
  <p>Seniors aged 65 and older receive half-price day passes at every pool.</p>
  <p>Garden plots are assigned by lottery each February; returning gardeners keep their plot.</p>
  <p>Permits are checked at the launch; a permit is not needed for the swim beach.</p>
  <p>Groups of twenty or more should book through the recreation office, not online.</p>
  <p>Weather closures are announced by 7 a.m. on the district status line and website.</p>
</div>
